# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sign-in — Sign in with Google (OpenID Connect identity token)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The site is static files on a bucket: it has no server, so it cannot keep a
# client secret, and it does not have one. What it uses instead is the flow
# Google designed for exactly that position — Google Identity Services hands the
# browser a signed identity token and nothing else. No authorization code, no
# token exchange, no access token, and nothing that could be used to reach into
# anyone's Google account.
#
# The one value below is an identifier, not a credential. It is compiled into
# the bundle and served to readers, which is fine and expected.
#
# In Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials, create an OAuth
# client ID of type "Web application" and list every origin the site is served
# from under *Authorized JavaScript origins* — they are compared as exact
# strings, scheme and port included:
#
#   http://localhost:4321
#   https://omnidynamics.dev
#   https://isahalim.github.io
#
# No redirect URI is needed: nothing redirects. If the client also has a client
# secret, nothing here uses it — delete it in the console rather than leave a
# live credential lying around.
#
# In CI this is a repository *variable*, set under Settings → Secrets and
# variables → Actions → Variables. Both workflows already read it.
PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Book a demo — Cal.com
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://github.com/calcom/cal.com (AGPL-3.0). The call is held on Cal Video,
# Cal's own room and the location a new event type already carries — nothing to
# connect, and no meeting provider beyond the one taking the booking. Pointing
# an event type at Google Meet or anything else is a setting on the event, with
# nothing to change in this repository; the site's copy names Cal Video, so
# change the copy too if you change the room.
#
# team/slug or user/slug of the event type — the path of the booking URL with
# no leading slash, so https://cal.com/s-halim-0296y9/30min is
# `s-halim-0296y9/30min`. That link is the default in `src/lib/auth/config.ts`;
# set this only to point the site at a different event type.
PUBLIC_CAL_LINK=
# Point this at your own instance if you self-host. Defaults to cal.com.
PUBLIC_CAL_ORIGIN=https://cal.com
